    "source_preservation": "The fixture includes a UTF-8 BOM, CRLF line endings, an unsupported wiki embed, and an unknown extension. Its expected result appends source text while retaining all existing bytes and unsupported syntax literally."
  },
  "contract": "A complete valid UTF-8 note of at most 16 KiB can be edited as explicit plain Markdown source. Saving uses the revision captured by the complete preview and the existing revision-checked vault writer. BOM, CRLF, and unsupported source syntax remain literal. A stale write preserves the external note, records the edited source in conflict recovery history, invalidates the preview revision, and disables another save until the source is read again.",
  "implementation": {
    "ui_layer": "The native source preview exposes an explicit multiline source draft with save and cancel actions. Draft mode blocks conflicting vault operations and navigation; truncated or revisionless previews cannot be edited. Successful saves retain the preview through refresh while the selected file still matches the saved revision; a later external change clears it.",
    "vault_layer": "Source bytes are submitted through the existing revision-checked writer. A stale revision is rejected and handled by existing conflict recovery; no unguarded write path or Markdown normalization was added.",
    "fixture": "The source-editing fixture records the exact source and exact expected post-edit source, including BOM, CRLF, unsupported wiki syntax, and an unknown extension.",
    "documentation": "The Markdown preview architecture and UI copy describe explicit plain-source editing, the 16 KiB bound, revision matching, unsupported syntax, and stale-save behavior."
  },
  "focused_tests": {
